WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.288 --> 00:00:01.541
- Good morning believe nation.

00:00:01.541 --> 00:00:04.839
Today's message is focus on happiness.

00:00:04.839 --> 00:00:06.501
Over to you Zendaya.

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.632
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.632 --> 00:00:11.337
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.337 --> 00:00:13.926
♫ Entspresso get me going

00:00:13.926 --> 00:00:18.227
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.227 --> 00:00:21.608
- Well the best thing I've
learned and advice I could give

00:00:21.608 --> 00:00:24.106
maybe my younger self is
really to focus on happiness.

00:00:24.106 --> 00:00:26.393
You know, happiness is
a key, because there's

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.262
so many people that you see,
that are in this industry,

00:00:28.262 --> 00:00:30.062
or just in life in general,
that are going through

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:33.359
their days and may have
everything they could ever want,

00:00:33.359 --> 00:00:35.031
but they're not happy, you know?

00:00:35.031 --> 00:00:36.494
So you have to focus
on what makes you happy

00:00:36.494 --> 00:00:40.162
and make decisions in
your career and your life

00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:41.869
that make you happy.

00:00:41.869 --> 00:00:43.367
And so I've been trying to do that

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:44.667
and it's working, you know.

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:47.871
And saying no to things that are negative.

00:00:47.871 --> 00:00:51.087
And saying no to things you
don't want to do, you know?

00:00:51.087 --> 00:00:54.512
So I think that's my
biggest piece of advice.

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:58.679
Something I try to do every
day is I try to make someone,

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.303
whether it be my team or
in my life or whatever,

00:01:02.303 --> 00:01:03.136
just happy.

00:01:03.136 --> 00:01:06.691
Or I try to make them feel
good or feel comfortable

00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:08.978
or feel loved, whatever it may be.

00:01:08.978 --> 00:01:10.441
It could be the littlest thing.

00:01:10.441 --> 00:01:13.030
It could be just saying, oh
you look really pretty today.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:16.525
Or it could be something
even smaller than that.

00:01:16.525 --> 00:01:18.324
Or something bigger than that, you know.

00:01:18.324 --> 00:01:21.030
It doesn't really matter
but it's just making

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.910
conscious effort to
make someone feel good.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.163
And that could be a stranger
or it could be your mom,

00:01:25.163 --> 00:01:26.329
you know.

00:01:26.329 --> 00:01:28.001
- I think this is a
really important message.

00:01:28.001 --> 00:01:30.753
I don't think entrepreneurs
focus on happiness enough.

00:01:30.753 --> 00:01:34.549
And I think when I am most
creative, when I am in the zone

00:01:34.549 --> 00:01:37.343
the most, when I'm working on
things that have the biggest

00:01:37.343 --> 00:01:39.851
returns, it's when I'm happiest.

00:01:39.851 --> 00:01:41.975
I thrive when I'm happy.

00:01:41.975 --> 00:01:44.599
I do my best work when I'm happy.

00:01:44.599 --> 00:01:45.981
And so I think it's
important to try to be there

00:01:45.981 --> 00:01:48.233
as much as possible.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:50.184
Now the next question,
which becomes harder,

00:01:50.184 --> 00:01:52.436
is well, how do you stay
happy, how do you get happy

00:01:52.436 --> 00:01:53.527
and how do you stay there.

00:01:53.527 --> 00:01:55.362
And we've done entire videos just on that.

00:01:55.362 --> 00:01:57.359
But I think the answer
ultimately comes down

00:01:57.359 --> 00:01:58.787
to self-acceptance.

00:01:58.787 --> 00:02:01.120
I think that the more
that you love yourself

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.535
and accept yourself for who you are,

00:02:03.535 --> 00:02:06.461
and not just accepting
to be like, well that's

00:02:06.461 --> 00:02:10.246
all I'm ever going to be,
but like love yourself.

00:02:10.246 --> 00:02:13.218
I love these things about myself.

00:02:13.218 --> 00:02:16.457
This thing that everybody
thinks I'm crazy about,

00:02:16.457 --> 00:02:18.175
like he's crazy, 'cause he does that,

00:02:18.175 --> 00:02:19.963
I love that about myself.

00:02:19.963 --> 00:02:23.667
When you love yourself,
then what happens is

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:27.394
you stop doing things
because of other people.

00:02:27.394 --> 00:02:32.061
You stop chasing something
because you want to look good

00:02:32.061 --> 00:02:35.648
for somebody else, because you
want to just beat that person,

00:02:35.648 --> 00:02:38.446
because you want to please somebody else.

00:02:38.446 --> 00:02:41.349
The less you care about
other peoples' opinions

00:02:41.349 --> 00:02:45.157
and judgments and expectations,
the less you care about

00:02:45.157 --> 00:02:48.326
that stuff, and the more
you focus on yourself

00:02:48.326 --> 00:02:51.542
and what makes you come alive,
and what you want to do,

00:02:51.542 --> 00:02:54.665
and be willing to shield yourself.

00:02:54.665 --> 00:02:56.384
It doesn't have to be in an arrogant way.

00:02:56.384 --> 00:02:58.590
Like you don't have to put somebody down

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.051
when they have expectations of you, right?

00:03:01.051 --> 00:03:02.885
When they think you should be doing that,

00:03:02.885 --> 00:03:04.600
and you say, well who
are you to tell me that.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.678
Right? You don't have to put them down.

00:03:06.678 --> 00:03:09.720
But it also doesn't have
to impact you, you know.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.018
I love that you guys all
have different opinions

00:03:12.018 --> 00:03:14.607
on what I should do,
and what I should wear

00:03:14.607 --> 00:03:17.440
and where I should go and
what my goal should be.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.600
I love that it always, for the most part,

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.155
comes from a place of love.

00:03:21.155 --> 00:03:24.232
It's like what you would do
if you were in my position.

00:03:24.232 --> 00:03:26.357
But at the same time,

00:03:26.357 --> 00:03:31.082
I'm not doing this because
you guys want me to.

00:03:31.082 --> 00:03:32.963
I'm doing the thing I want to do,

00:03:32.963 --> 00:03:34.832
that makes me happy.

00:03:34.832 --> 00:03:38.594
And when you love yourself,
when you accept yourself

00:03:38.594 --> 00:03:41.635
and love yourself, then
it makes you happier.

00:03:41.635 --> 00:03:43.052
At least that makes me happier.

00:03:43.052 --> 00:03:45.095
And so I'd strongly
encourage you to examine

00:03:45.095 --> 00:03:46.465
the work that you're doing.

00:03:46.465 --> 00:03:49.135
Why are you taking on
this project or going down

00:03:49.135 --> 00:03:50.564
that path.

00:03:50.564 --> 00:03:52.479
Who are you doing it for?

00:03:52.479 --> 00:03:54.360
Are you doing it just for somebody else?

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.985
Are you doing it because
you don't want to look bad

00:03:55.985 --> 00:03:57.564
in front of somebody else?

00:03:57.564 --> 00:03:59.643
Are you doing it because
you're just trying

00:03:59.643 --> 00:04:02.603
to boost your ego up or
to have a great picture

00:04:02.603 --> 00:04:05.064
that you can post on
Facebook or Instagram?

00:04:05.064 --> 00:04:06.574
Are you doing it because
your parents want you

00:04:06.574 --> 00:04:07.746
to do it?

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:09.917
Or because you're just
trying to beat somebody else?

00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:13.412
Or are you doing it because
you had the fire to do it.

00:04:13.412 --> 00:04:15.629
You're doing it because you
need to express yourself

00:04:15.629 --> 00:04:18.544
and you got to let this thing come out.

00:04:18.544 --> 00:04:20.552
I'd strongly encourage
you to examine the reasons

00:04:20.552 --> 00:04:22.468
why you're doing the work.

00:04:22.468 --> 00:04:25.997
And if too many of your
projects are outward focused,

00:04:25.997 --> 00:04:29.260
instead of I love doing
this, then you aren't really

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:30.560
going to be happy.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.393
And you're not really going
to create something amazing.

00:04:33.393 --> 00:04:35.274
So flip the switch.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:38.188
Make for yourself and be happy.

00:04:38.188 --> 00:04:40.405
So the question of the day today is

00:04:40.405 --> 00:04:42.031
are you happy?

00:04:42.031 --> 00:04:44.991
Are you happy with the
work that you're doing?

00:04:44.991 --> 00:04:46.152
Leave it in the comments below.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.612
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:04:47.612 --> 00:04:49.702
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Luke Marcus

00:04:49.702 --> 00:04:50.991
Jon Kroeger.

00:04:50.991 --> 00:04:52.953
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:04:52.953 --> 00:04:53.870
Your One Word.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:56.576
It really really really
really means a lot to me.

00:04:56.576 --> 00:04:58.007
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:58.007 --> 00:04:59.249
I believe in you.

00:04:59.249 --> 00:05:01.386
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:01.386 --> 00:05:03.673
and whatever your one
word is, and I'll see you

00:05:03.673 --> 00:05:07.016
again tomorrow morning for
another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:07.016 --> 00:05:09.722
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:05:09.722 --> 00:05:13.120
♫ Entspresso get me going.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.057
For those of you who want
to learn a little bit more

00:05:15.057 --> 00:05:16.984
about how to focus on
happiness, here are some

00:05:16.984 --> 00:05:18.772
extra bonus clips.

00:05:18.772 --> 00:05:20.026
Hope you enjoy.

00:05:20.026 --> 00:05:22.905
You want the flashy things,
until you know, you grow older,

00:05:22.905 --> 00:05:24.476
you know as an adult and you'll be able

00:05:24.476 --> 00:05:26.659
to understand yourself a little bit more.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:29.155
I learned that them things
didn't make me happy.

00:05:29.155 --> 00:05:33.451
I learned that, you know, that
really money really don't...

00:05:33.451 --> 00:05:35.668
I'm learning that now, you
know, that's not really

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:38.873
my peace of mind, having money.

00:05:38.873 --> 00:05:40.800
You know, that's something
I learned this year.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.634
Then years before that
I learned that jewelry

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:45.386
and all that stuff doesn't make me happy.

00:05:45.386 --> 00:05:48.056
And when you learn that,
you'll be able to grow

00:05:48.056 --> 00:05:50.216
more as a person, you know.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:51.934
What makes me happy is
really challenging myself

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:55.185
and knowing that I defeated my last goal

00:05:55.185 --> 00:05:59.562
and took myself to the next
level as a better person.

00:05:59.562 --> 00:06:01.651
- What's success anyway?

00:06:01.651 --> 00:06:03.822
Is success about making the most money?

00:06:03.822 --> 00:06:05.401
No, not, no.

00:06:05.401 --> 00:06:09.535
Money for the most part
turns people into jerks.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.915
If you do become rich,
the university fundraising

00:06:11.915 --> 00:06:13.447
and development office
will certainly want to stay

00:06:13.447 --> 00:06:14.782
in touch with you.

00:06:14.782 --> 00:06:15.746
(laughter)

00:06:15.746 --> 00:06:17.580
and if you give enough
money, you'll get your name

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.738
on a plaque above the
dirty laundry bin here

00:06:19.738 --> 00:06:21.671
in the men's locker room.

00:06:21.671 --> 00:06:23.332
But that still doesn't
make you a great person

00:06:23.332 --> 00:06:26.118
and it definitely doesn't
mean anyone will like you.

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:27.755
I mean don't get me wrong,
as I mentioned before,

00:06:27.755 --> 00:06:29.798
you're never going to feel
richer than when you've

00:06:29.798 --> 00:06:32.515
paid off those credit
cards and student loans.

00:06:32.515 --> 00:06:35.394
But after that, money tends
to be pretty unfulfilling.

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:39.017
Almost all the people I know
who've made a lot of money,

00:06:39.017 --> 00:06:42.140
they've turned into that guy,
alright, well you know the guy

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:45.530
who pops his collar, and
if it were up to him,

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:47.898
and he were wearing two shirts,
he could pop both collars.

00:06:47.898 --> 00:06:49.280
(laughter)

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:50.530
That's the guy.

00:06:52.496 --> 00:06:54.330
So how will we know when
we've done it right.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.072
What's the ultimate
measure of success then.

00:06:56.072 --> 00:06:58.127
What's the key to success?

00:06:58.127 --> 00:07:00.443
Well in my experience, quite simply,

00:07:00.443 --> 00:07:02.193
success is happiness.

00:07:03.625 --> 00:07:05.540
It all comes down to happiness.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.711
And I definitely don't mean
that happiness that you feel

00:07:07.711 --> 00:07:10.414
when the Gophers take over on
downs in their own red zone,

00:07:10.414 --> 00:07:12.551
as great as that feels.

00:07:12.551 --> 00:07:14.675
I mean that happiness
that quite literally fills

00:07:14.675 --> 00:07:16.301
your lungs.

00:07:16.301 --> 00:07:18.309
The kind of happiness that make a noise.

00:07:18.309 --> 00:07:20.271
It announces its arrival
with a deep inhale

00:07:20.271 --> 00:07:22.059
and a deep exhale.

00:07:22.059 --> 00:07:23.986
(deep breath)

00:07:23.986 --> 00:07:27.272
That happiness. You know
that happiness, right?

00:07:27.272 --> 00:07:30.279
That happiness is success,
because it turns out,

00:07:30.279 --> 00:07:32.787
happy people get jobs.

00:07:32.787 --> 00:07:36.200
Happy people create. Happy people win.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.290
Happy people fall in
love and raise families.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.589
They lead and change the world.

00:07:40.589 --> 00:07:43.213
Happy people get what
they want because often

00:07:43.213 --> 00:07:45.836
happy people are the ones
who realize they don't really

00:07:45.836 --> 00:07:47.624
need much more than they already
have, and they appreciate

00:07:47.624 --> 00:07:49.377
what they've got.

00:07:49.377 --> 00:07:51.966
Happy people are contagious.

00:07:51.966 --> 00:07:53.882
- She's worried about the rent, okay.

00:07:53.882 --> 00:07:56.515
She's a single mother.
She's worried about her kid.

00:07:56.515 --> 00:07:57.641
- You know, there's nuttin'
you can do about the rent

00:07:57.641 --> 00:07:58.477
from worrying about it.

00:07:58.477 --> 00:07:59.847
That ain't going to get you no rent.

00:07:59.847 --> 00:08:01.681
Presence and happiness gets you rent.

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:03.260
Money can't make you happy.

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:04.433
But happy can make you money.

00:08:04.433 --> 00:08:06.151
So be happy. Go out in the world.

00:08:06.151 --> 00:08:08.485
There's a story of a
guy in a shanty house.

00:08:08.485 --> 00:08:12.409
He rolls over in the morning, meditates,

00:08:12.409 --> 00:08:14.359
goes out into the world, and is like, damn

00:08:14.359 --> 00:08:16.867
I'm going to have to
get some bread and water

00:08:16.867 --> 00:08:18.075
'fore the whole shht go down.

00:08:18.075 --> 00:08:20.118
Before I get back in that bed.

00:08:20.118 --> 00:08:23.496
But in the meantime, be
nice to all my neighbors

00:08:23.496 --> 00:08:25.377
in the shanty village.

00:08:25.377 --> 00:08:26.942
Everybody is suffering
in what everybody else

00:08:26.942 --> 00:08:28.084
calls extreme poverty.

00:08:28.084 --> 00:08:32.128
But he's happy. He doesn't
have a poverty mindset.

00:08:32.128 --> 00:08:34.307
Nor is he worried about
that bread and water.

00:08:34.307 --> 00:08:35.723
They going to give me
some mother f'n bread,

00:08:35.723 --> 00:08:37.383
I'm ain't going to worry about that shht.

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:38.800
Cause I'm that dude.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.178
He walks out, smiling,
confident, comfortable.

00:08:42.178 --> 00:08:43.339
He gets what he needs.

00:08:43.339 --> 00:08:45.557
He says, but Yogananda
would say God will provide,

00:08:45.557 --> 00:08:48.320
but really, you're god,
you're working to get

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.108
and it shows up.

00:08:50.108 --> 00:08:51.443
He gets his bread and water.

00:08:51.443 --> 00:08:52.407
He makes everybody happy.

00:08:52.407 --> 00:08:53.742
Everybody makes him
happy. He lays in the bed.

00:08:53.742 --> 00:08:58.492
The next nigga, he wakes
up, he's got 36 billion

00:08:58.492 --> 00:08:59.832
dollars in the bank.

00:08:59.832 --> 00:09:01.573
He gets up, the stock
market goes up, he says

00:09:01.573 --> 00:09:03.631
oh, shht, he gets some
coke, he gets some alcohol,

00:09:03.631 --> 00:09:04.948
he's gets happy, he's so excited.

00:09:04.948 --> 00:09:07.456
I'm exploding. I'm making more
money, mo' money, mo' money.

00:09:07.456 --> 00:09:10.288
Oh shht, crashed, oh shht
more cocaine, more alcohol.

00:09:10.288 --> 00:09:12.256
Oh shht, I'm f*cked up, I'm f*cked up.

00:09:12.256 --> 00:09:14.506
His heart goes up and down.

00:09:16.134 --> 00:09:20.301
And he dies at 40. The shanty
house guy lived to 100.

00:09:21.556 --> 00:09:23.228
The other guy's diet...

00:09:23.228 --> 00:09:25.097
Not the diet the other guy
took, but the other guy's

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:26.943
opportunity was probably a greater diet,

00:09:26.943 --> 00:09:30.012
the guy in the shanty house
would've made it to 120,

00:09:30.012 --> 00:09:32.111
but you know, he made 100.

00:09:32.111 --> 00:09:33.237
This guy died at 40.

00:09:33.237 --> 00:09:37.823
That's the reality. Our
happiness is up to us.

00:09:37.823 --> 00:09:40.331
Our relationship with
the world is up to us.

00:09:40.331 --> 00:09:44.580
Our anxiety is controlled
or given to us by us.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:47.332
- What Seneca is saying,
and all the Stoics,

00:09:47.332 --> 00:09:48.748
they're not saying you can't be wealthy,

00:09:48.748 --> 00:09:51.175
you can't be successful, you
can't go out and do things.

00:09:51.175 --> 00:09:55.342
What they're saying is
that, you can't be dependent

00:09:56.678 --> 00:09:57.932
on these things.

00:09:57.932 --> 00:10:00.428
He's saying, wealth is
nice if you have it.

00:10:00.428 --> 00:10:03.017
But if you make your
personal happiness dependent

00:10:03.017 --> 00:10:06.477
on having this money,
that's bad, because it's not

00:10:06.477 --> 00:10:07.893
in your control, right?

00:10:07.893 --> 00:10:09.727
The economy can melt down at any moment.

00:10:09.727 --> 00:10:11.481
Or your house could burn down.

00:10:11.481 --> 00:10:13.025
Or you could lose your job.

00:10:13.025 --> 00:10:17.448
And if you have equated wealth
with personal happiness,

00:10:17.448 --> 00:10:21.036
now your personal happiness
is outside of your control.

00:10:21.036 --> 00:10:23.578
And so stoicism is about
control in that sense.

00:10:23.578 --> 00:10:27.661
How do you make the
distinction between externals

00:10:28.582 --> 00:10:31.334
and internals and focus
most of your energy

00:10:31.334 --> 00:10:32.622
on internals.

00:10:32.622 --> 00:10:35.629
Having externals is nice,
but sort of what they

00:10:35.629 --> 00:10:38.346
would say, is understand
that they're yours in trust.

00:10:38.346 --> 00:10:41.341
Which means that they could
leave you at any moment.

00:10:41.341 --> 00:10:43.129
And a lot of the stoic exercises are about

00:10:43.129 --> 00:10:45.846
practicing not having those things.

00:10:45.846 --> 00:10:48.691
So Seneca was famous he, one day a month,

00:10:48.691 --> 00:10:50.525
he would practice being poor.

00:10:50.525 --> 00:10:53.776
So he would wear crappy
clothes and he would not

00:10:53.776 --> 00:10:56.064
eat at his house and
he would sleep outside.

00:10:56.064 --> 00:10:59.826
I think it's more now a
metaphor than anything else.

00:10:59.826 --> 00:11:03.529
But the idea is we're so
afraid of these things,

00:11:03.529 --> 00:11:05.747
so we don't think about
them, and therefore we're not

00:11:05.747 --> 00:11:09.497
prepared for them, and then
it makes them much scarier

00:11:09.497 --> 00:11:12.631
and we dread them that
much more, even though

00:11:12.631 --> 00:11:15.128
if you looked at it really objectively,

00:11:15.128 --> 00:11:16.741
it's really not that bad.

00:11:16.741 --> 00:11:19.296
- I had a dream to come to Barcelona,

00:11:19.296 --> 00:11:22.256
but afterwards I'm
thinking maybe you should

00:11:22.256 --> 00:11:25.844
keep your dream, instead
of making it come true.

00:11:25.844 --> 00:11:28.857
Because that dream could
almost, not almost,

00:11:28.857 --> 00:11:30.847
could have, not destroyed me,

00:11:30.847 --> 00:11:33.692
but make it difficult for me.

00:11:33.692 --> 00:11:35.735
And the first six months, fantastic.

00:11:35.735 --> 00:11:37.523
I had a fantastic time.

00:11:37.523 --> 00:11:40.065
I had a very good
relationship with Guardiola.

00:11:40.065 --> 00:11:42.577
I wanted to learn the
Barcelona, the way of playing.

00:11:42.577 --> 00:11:44.237
I played good the first six months.

00:11:44.237 --> 00:11:46.164
After that, something
happened that I still don't

00:11:46.164 --> 00:11:50.820
have answers for, which
maybe I will never know.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:53.293
I mean if somebody has a problem with me,

00:11:53.293 --> 00:11:54.790
they should come to me
and we will resolve it,

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:56.613
whatever the problem is, like a man.

00:11:56.613 --> 00:11:59.260
Because it was ridiculous,
you don't talk to the player.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:02.255
The player is looking for answers.

00:12:02.255 --> 00:12:04.589
At that moment, I was not happy.

00:12:04.589 --> 00:12:06.632
And I said, I have to choose.

00:12:06.632 --> 00:12:10.766
Either I stay, win everything,
but I will not be happy.

00:12:10.766 --> 00:12:13.355
Or I got to somewhere else.

00:12:13.355 --> 00:12:14.225
And that is what happened.

00:12:14.225 --> 00:12:15.607
I went to Milan.

00:12:15.607 --> 00:12:19.148
My joy came back for playing football.

00:12:19.148 --> 00:12:21.698
I did a good job. I won
the Scudetto immediately.

00:12:21.698 --> 00:12:23.532
I won the Super Cup.

00:12:23.532 --> 00:12:28.327
Everybody was happy and they
were like appreciating me

00:12:28.327 --> 00:12:29.234
for playing there.

